{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And now, set your heart:</b> The meaning of ומעלה — the day that comes after this, as in \"from twenty years old and upward\" (Numbers 1:3 etc.). The word כי is lacking." "<b>Before a stone was set:</b> וטרם ישרת serves in place of אחר. And so it is: before the stones became the foundation of the temple — everyone who came to the heap of grain, and those who reckoned would find in it twenty measures, and behold, half — for the curse was upon it." "<b>The word לחשוף:</b> water from a cistern, like לדלות. And behold, the curse — that they would find in it less than half of what they reckoned."], :book :haggai, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra explains the phrase מיום ומעלה in the verse; the lemma heading reflects the opening words of the comment, not the phrase under discussion.", 2 "Possible textual corruption in והנה המארה שימצאו בה; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Haggai" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/hagai"] ["Ibn Ezra on Haggai -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/hagai"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:33.876428509Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}